{
  "title": "6W6",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "TR-606 style drum",
        "machine. Every voice",
        "synthesized, no",
        "samples - kick,",
        "snare, toms, hats,",
        "cymbal, plus a clap.",
        "Fitted to a real 606.",
        "",
        "Reverb + delay sends",
        "on every voice.",
        "7 distortion types",
        "per voice and on the",
        "master. Comp on the",
        "master bus."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Playing",
      "lines": [
        "Pads (left 4x4):",
        " row1: BD SD LT HT",
        " row2: CH OH CY CP",
        " pad 9:  Master",
        " pad10:  Reverb",
        " pad11:  Delay",
        "",
        "Shift+Pad: select",
        " without sounding.",
        "Mute+Pad: mute that",
        " drum ([M] in bar)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Editing",
      "lines": [
        "Knobs 1-8 edit the",
        "visible page.",
        "Jog: change page.",
        "Jog CLICK on Main:",
        " lock it, so pads",
        " stop moving the",
        " page ([L] in bar).",
        "Shift: values + fine",
        "Mute+knob: default",
        "",
        "Delete or Copy held:",
        " pads go straight to",
        " Move, so you can",
        " clear steps on any",
        " pad, page pads too."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Distortion",
      "lines": [
        "Drive + a type on",
        "every voice, and",
        "again on the master:",
        " DIODE the machine's",
        " CLIP  asymmetric",
        " SAT   warm, parallel",
        " BFZ   fuzz wall",
        " PDIST cubic crunch",
        " FOLD  wavefolder",
        " CRUSH bits + rate",
        "",
        "Drive fully DOWN is",
        "exactly dry - the",
        "stage is not in the",
        "path at all."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Velocity",
      "lines": [
        "Velocity sets the",
        "level, all the way",
        "up - no accent",
        "switch, no step in",
        "the middle. A hit at",
        "127 is the loudest",
        "the kit gets.",
        "",
        "VELOCITY on Master",
        "is how far a soft",
        "hit falls below it:",
        "0 = every hit the",
        "same, full = the",
        "widest range. It",
        "only carves DOWN,",
        "never boosts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Snare",
      "lines": [
        "Decay shortens the",
        "WHOLE drum, body and",
        "wires: 2.5 ms fully",
        "down, 141 ms at the",
        "default, 370 ms wide",
        "open (the natural",
        "606 tail).",
        "",
        "The machine has no",
        "such knob - default",
        "is the fitted 606",
        "value, so the stock",
        "kit is unchanged.",
        "",
        "Tone gave up its",
        "encoder for it (8 is",
        "all there is). It is",
        "still on the web",
        "panel and as an LFO",
        "target."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Hats",
      "lines": [
        "Choke (Cl Hat page",
        "and Master):",
        " Off - hats ring",
        "  over each other",
        " CH > OH - closed",
        "  cuts open (606)",
        " Mutual - either",
        "  cuts the other"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Send FX",
      "lines": [
        "Rev and Dly on every",
        "voice are SENDS: turn",
        "them up, then set the",
        "bus on pads 10 / 11.",
        "",
        "Delay Time is a note",
        "division and follows",
        "the host tempo, so it",
        "stays in time when",
        "you change BPM.",
        "",
        "Both are silent at",
        "zero - the kit is",
        "untouched until you",
        "send something."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sequencing",
      "lines": [
        "Use Move's own",
        "sequencer: drum",
        "track with a kit,",
        "mute it (HiJack),",
        "set track MIDI OUT",
        "to the slot channel.",
        "Each drum = one",
        "lane. Note map:",
        "drum rack 36-43",
        "(or GM, switchable)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Remote UI",
      "lines": [
        "Full panel in the",
        "browser: EVERY",
        "control at once, all",
        "8 voices plus the",
        "buses and master.",
        "",
        "Port 7700 on the",
        "Move's address, then",
        " /remote-ui",
        " move.local:7700",
        " 172.16.254.1:7700",
        "  (USB-C, always)",
        "",
        "The voice you are on",
        "here is highlighted",
        "there. Double-click",
        "a knob to reset it."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
